## The Short Answer on Thanksgiving Nails This Year

A shorter nail bed was never the limitation the long-nail roundups implied. **Short thanksgiving nails** hold colour, finish, and a single well-placed motif with just as much intention as anything built for a longer set, and they do it while surviving an actual hosting day better. The shape decision comes first, squoval or short oval for anyone spending the day cooking or serving, and every design choice after that works with the canvas rather than fighting it.

What separates a set that looks deliberate from one that looks shrunk down is restraint. One motif, not five. A scaled line, not a shrunk one. A finish that carries the whole look instead of a pattern trying to do too much on too little space. That is the entire method behind every design in this edit, and it holds up across shape, colour, and technique far better than treating short nails as an afterthought ever could. This is a Thanksgiving manicure built for the nails you actually have, not a compromise version of someone else's.
